body:
This patch removes the transient FS capability shim from `InputSource` instantiation and re-normalizes path resolution onto the preexisting source-type dispatch contract.

The current constructor path has effectively grown a policy-bearing side channel: `InputSource.__new__()` is forwarding opaque kwargs into concrete source backends, and `FileInputSource` is now carrying chroot state plus path rebasing semantics that are orthogonal to the object’s core responsibility (source adaptation and line retrieval). That introduces a leaky capability boundary in the I/O stack and couples call-site policy to backend object materialization.

Concretely, the kwargs fan-out changes the allocation ABI for all `InputSource` subclasses, forcing every dispatch target to tolerate policy metadata despite only `FileInputSource` consuming it. In practice this widens the constructor surface, complicates subclass invariants, and makes source selection sensitive to higher-layer execution context rather than source identity. Reverting to the narrower ctor contract restores the intended discriminant-only dispatch path (`-`, `https:`, local file) and keeps backend initialization free of ambient policy flags.

On the file backend, the chroot/rebase layer is also doing path authority enforcement inside `FileInputSource.__init__()` and `relative()`. That is the wrong stratum for this logic: `relative()` should remain a pure locator transform over the backing source, not a policy-preserving capability propagator. Carrying `chrootPath` through recursive relative resolution effectively turns `FileInputSource` into a stateful confinement token, which is inconsistent with the rest of the loader pipeline and makes path derivation semantics depend on constructor provenance.

Relatedly, `config.chrootPath()` injects process-global diagnostics into a low-level path canonicalization path. Emitting `messages.die()` from config-level path normalization folds policy failure, UX/reporting, and path math into a single helper, which is hostile to composability and difficult to reason about in non-top-level retrieval flows.

This patch therefore:

- removes kwargs propagation from `InputSource.__new__()` dispatch;
- collapses `FileInputSource` back to a single-source-name initializer;
- drops chroot-state retention from `FileInputSource.relative()`;
- removes the CLI/global constant plumbing for FS confinement/execute capability toggles that were only supporting this constructor-path policy injection;
- simplifies `retrieveBoilerplateFile()` back to ordinary `InputSource(...)` construction for non-local boilerplate sources;
- deletes the config-level chroot path gate so config helpers remain path utilities rather than policy/reporting endpoints.

Net effect is a cleaner separation between source adaptation, boilerplate retrieval, and top-level runtime policy, with fewer ambient flags crossing subsystem boundaries and a restored minimal ctor ABI for the input pipeline.

